<protocol name="multi_item_image" type="exploration" domain="shared">

## PURPOSE

Domain-agnostic pattern for handling images containing multiple distinct items.
Applies universally: products, properties, dishes, garments, components, or any future domain.

This protocol defines the PATTERN. Domain-specific protocols apply the VOCABULARY.

---

## CORE CONCEPTS

### Item
A distinct, identifiable entity within an image that could be processed independently.

| Domain | "Item" Means |
|--------|--------------|
| Catalog | Product, variant |
| Real Estate | Room, property feature |
| Food | Dish, ingredient |
| Fashion | Garment, accessory |
| Manufacturing | Component, part |
| Events | Person, object |
| **Any Future** | Whatever discrete entities exist |

### Classification Types

| Type | Definition | Examples |
|------|------------|----------|
| **VARIANTS** | Same item type, different attributes | 3 jar sizes, 4 shirt colors, 3 room angles |
| **COLLECTION** | Different item types, related context | Product + accessories, dish + sides, outfit + accessories |
| **COMPONENTS** | Parts of a single whole | Disassembled product, floor plan sections |
| **UNRELATED** | Coincidental presence | Background clutter, bystanders |

### Variant Axes

When items are VARIANTS, identify the axes of variation:

| Axis Type | Examples |
|-----------|----------|
| Size | Small/Medium/Large, 250ml/500ml/1L |
| Color | Red/Blue/Green, Oak/Walnut/White |
| Design | Pattern A/B/C, Style 1/2/3 |
| Material | Glass/Plastic/Metal |
| Configuration | 2-door/4-door, 1BR/2BR |

---

## ITEM MANIFEST FORMAT (CRITICAL OUTPUT)

When multi-item detected, output a structured manifest that downstream agents can act on:

```markdown
## MULTI-ITEM ASSESSMENT

- **Count:** [N]
- **Classification:** [VARIANTS | COLLECTION | COMPONENTS | UNRELATED]
- **Rationale:** [Why this classification]

### Variant Axes (if VARIANTS)

| Axis | Values |
|------|--------|
| [axis1] | [value1, value2, value3] |
| [axis2] | [valueA, valueB] |

### Extraction Targets

| # | Description | Position | Key Attributes |
|---|-------------|----------|----------------|
| 1 | [what it is] | [where in frame] | [domain-specific attributes] |
| 2 | [what it is] | [where in frame] | [domain-specific attributes] |
| ... | ... | ... | ... |

**Note:** Domain protocols extend "Key Attributes" with domain-specific columns (e.g., Size, Color for catalog).

### Processing Strategies

| Strategy | Result | Recommended When |
|----------|--------|------------------|
| INDIVIDUAL | [N] separate outputs | [context] |
| BY_[AXIS] | [M] grouped outputs | [context] |
| COMPOSITE | 1 combined output | [context] |

**Default recommendation:** [STRATEGY] because [reasoning]
```

### Position Vocabulary (Universal)

Use consistent position descriptors across all domains:

| Position | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| top-left, top-center, top-right | Upper third of frame |
| middle-left, center, middle-right | Middle third of frame |
| bottom-left, bottom-center, bottom-right | Lower third of frame |
| foreground, midground, background | Depth positioning |
| left-column, center-column, right-column | Columnar arrangement |
| row-1, row-2, row-3 | Row arrangement |

---

## PROCESSING STRATEGIES

### INDIVIDUAL

Extract each item separately, producing N outputs.

**When to use:**
- Catalog/inventory work (each SKU needs its own asset)
- Portfolio items (each piece showcased independently)
- Detailed documentation (each component documented)

**Execution pattern:**
```
for each item in manifest:
    process(target="{item.description} at {item.position}")
    output: one asset per item
```

### GROUPED (BY_AXIS)

Group items by a variant axis, producing M outputs (M < N).

**When to use:**
- Size comparison graphics (group by size)
- Color swatches (group by color)
- Category showcases (group by type)

**Execution pattern:**
```
for each group in manifest.group_by(axis):
    process(targets=group.items)
    output: one asset per group
```

### COMPOSITE

Keep all items together in arrangement, producing 1 output.

**When to use:**
- Family/range shots (show the full collection)
- Lifestyle scenes (items in context together)
- Marketing banners (complete offering)

**Execution pattern:**
```
process(all_items, preserve_arrangement=True)
output: one combined asset
```

### SELECTIVE

Filter to specific items, then apply INDIVIDUAL or COMPOSITE.

**When to use:**
- User requests specific items ("just the large ones")
- Quality filtering ("only the sharp ones")
- Relevance filtering ("only the food items, not the props")

**Execution pattern:**
```
filtered = manifest.filter(criteria)
then: INDIVIDUAL or COMPOSITE on filtered
```

#### SELECTIVE Parsing

When user requests a subset, parse filter criteria from their words:

| User Says | Filter Attribute | Match Pattern |
|-----------|------------------|---------------|
| "only the large ones" | Size | Size = "Large" |
| "just the blue ones" | Color/Design | Color = "Blue" OR Design contains "blue" |
| "the ones in the top row" | Position | Position starts with "top-" |
| "middle size only" | Size | Size = "Medium" |
| "the pink design" | Design | Design contains "pink" |

**Parsing template:**
```
User request: "only the large ones"

1. IDENTIFY filter: Size = "Large"
2. MATCH against Extraction Targets:
   - Item 1: Size=Large -> MATCH
   - Item 2: Size=Large -> MATCH
   - Item 4: Size=Medium -> NO MATCH
   ...
3. FILTERED SET: Items 1, 2, 3
4. APPLY strategy: INDIVIDUAL on filtered set
5. RESULT: 3 outputs (not 9)
```

---

## STRATEGY SELECTION SIGNALS

### From Task Description

| Signal in Task | Implies Strategy |
|----------------|------------------|
| "each", "individual", "per item", "separately" | INDIVIDUAL |
| "together", "family", "group", "all in one", "range" | COMPOSITE |
| "by size", "by color", "grouped by" | GROUPED |
| "only the X", "just the Y", "specific" | SELECTIVE |

### From Domain Context

| Domain Context | Default Strategy |
|----------------|------------------|
| Catalog, inventory, SKU creation | INDIVIDUAL |
| Marketing, lifestyle, campaigns | COMPOSITE |
| Comparison, sizing guide | GROUPED |
| Quality issue, specific request | SELECTIVE |

### Ambiguity Resolution

If signals are unclear:
1. Check if task explicitly mentions desired output count
2. Infer from domain context (catalog = individual, marketing = composite)
3. Ask for clarification with options

---

## WORKFLOW PATTERN

```
1. DETECT
   - View image, identify item count and relationships
   - Classify: VARIANTS / COLLECTION / COMPONENTS / UNRELATED

2. MANIFEST
   - Output structured item list with positions and attributes
   - Identify variant axes if applicable

3. STRATEGIZE
   - Read task signals for strategy preference
   - Apply domain defaults if no explicit signal
   - Document chosen strategy with rationale

4. EXECUTE
   - Apply strategy pattern (INDIVIDUAL / GROUPED / COMPOSITE / SELECTIVE)
   - Track progress through manifest

5. VERIFY
   - Confirm all intended items processed
   - Quality check each output
```

---

## FAILURE HANDLING

When extracting N items individually, some may fail. Handle gracefully.

### Failure Strategies

| Strategy | When | Behavior |
|----------|------|----------|
| **CONTINUE** (default) | Most cases | Complete remaining items, report failures at end |
| **RETRY_ONCE** | Ambiguous targeting | Retry failed item with refined description |
| **ABORT** | Critical dependency between items | Stop on first failure, return partial results |

### Result Reporting Format

When extraction completes (with or without failures), report structured results:

```markdown
## EXTRACTION RESULTS

- **Completed:** [X] of [N]
- **Failed:** [Y] (items: #5, #7)
- **Strategy used:** [INDIVIDUAL/COMPOSITE/etc.]

### Outputs

| # | Description | Output ID | Status | Notes |
|---|-------------|-----------|--------|-------|
| 1 | Large jar blue lid | asset_abc123 | SUCCESS | |
| 2 | Large jar yellow lid | asset_def456 | SUCCESS | |
| 5 | Medium jar blue lid | - | FAILED | Items overlap in source |
| 7 | Small jar blue lid | - | FAILED | Extraction ambiguous |

### Failure Details (if any)

| # | Reason | Recoverable |
|---|--------|-------------|
| 5 | Items overlap - can't isolate | Yes - retry with tighter targeting |
| 7 | Position descriptor too vague | Yes - use "bottom-left corner" |
```

### Recovery Guidance

| Failure Type | Recovery Action |
|--------------|-----------------|
| Overlap/ambiguous | Retry with more specific position: "the leftmost jar in bottom row" |
| Not found at position | Verify Extraction Targets against actual image |
| Quality issue | Retry with different extraction settings |
| Persistent failure | Report to PM, continue with successful items |

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Correct Approach |
|--------------|---------|------------------|
| Treating multi-item as single unit | "the jars" instead of "9 jars" | Enumerate each item explicitly |
| No position info | Can't target specific items | Always include position descriptors |
| Ignoring variant structure | Miss size/color relationships | Identify variant axes |
| Hardcoded strategy | Always INDIVIDUAL or always COMPOSITE | Select strategy from signals |
| No manifest output | Downstream agents can't act | Always produce structured manifest |

---

## DOMAIN APPLICATION

This protocol provides the PATTERN. Domain-specific protocols provide the VOCABULARY:

```
Domain Protocol includes multi_item_image.protocol:
- Maps "item" to domain entity (product, room, dish)
- Maps attributes to domain fields (size, sqft, portion)
- Applies domain-specific defaults
```

The pattern (classification, manifest, strategies) remains identical across domains.

</protocol>
